; A backslash in a string stands before any character. Beancount names
; five of them (a line break, a tab, a carriage return, a form feed and a
; backspace); before any other character it stands for that character,
; and is no error.
2020-01-01 open Assets:A
2020-01-02 note Assets:A "a\qb"
2020-01-03 note Assets:A "a\x41b"
2020-01-04 note Assets:A "a\/b \'c\' \0"
2020-01-05 note Assets:A "tab\there"
